      "writtenOn": "2024-04-05T19:04:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might be possible from one direction. I think we could add an assert that when Device is deleted it shouldn\u0027t have any pending work if it hasn\u0027t abandoned its recorder. If it did, that would mean that it wasn\u0027t manually flushed or had its owning surface go out of scope, or been marked immutable, etc, but also hadn\u0027t had abandonRecorder() called.\n\nHowever, there\u0027s not a good way to have `Recorder::snap()` check all un-registered devices to make sure they\u0027ve had their work flushed.\n\nFor now I\u0027m inclined to leave it as-is. My medium-term design hope is that scratch device tasks will be referenced by parent tasks and be ordered correctly there. This would be both for drawing a scratch device or copying from a scratch device. Operations that need to instantiate and return a scratch device to the client would have an explicit task added to the root task list that held on to the device\u0027s tasks and represents the conversion from scratch to not-scratch (e.g. SkImages::MakeWithFilter).  In that world, we wouldn\u0027t be dependent on surfaces going out of scope or manually flushing to order tasks appropriately.",
      "parentUuid": "9bb75a8d_167138f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 47,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "207bdc7d0e6e7f5953ddedac4e70597be5c01cc5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
